From bea6754372ec5cc55314d5988e70ff0d668497ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GibaxLeGrand <48137851+GibaxLeGrand@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:26:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Runner: the lobby's B (back to choosing), gear number and
 controls hint

On the waiting screen with SRNP_LOBBY=1: the local pad is read even once ready, and B sends UNREADY
(the relay puts the seat back to choosing and the race waits for it). Each card shows the gear chosen
("GEAR n": the gear table's names are not known yet; the race still corrects a gear the character may
not ride), and a line at the bottom gives this machine's seat its controls in the names' font
("LEFT/RIGHT CHARACTER  UP/DOWN GEAR  A READY", then "B BACK TO CHOOSING"; the font has "/" but no
":"). SRNP_LOBBY_AUTO=<c>/<g>/<s>/<b> tests B without a pad: ready, B <b> seconds later, ready again.
Measured with 3 runners: the relay logs ready, back to choosing, ready (30.5 s, 38.5 s, 46.5 s) and
starts once the last seat is ready; the race has the characters chosen; 39 identical checksums.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
